Division of the likelihood mapping plots into 3 or 7 areas.
On the left the areas show support for one of the different groupings
like (a,b|c,d).
On the right the right quartets falling into the areas 1, 2 and 3 are
informative. Those in the rectangles 4, 5 and 6 are partly informative
and those in the center (7) are not informative.

Sequences a,b,c,d are drawn from all included sequences.

Note, that the corners only make a difference if the sequences are
clustered in groups. Furthermore, while sequences should occur about
equally often in unclustered mappings, in clustered mappings their
occurrence rates depend on the group sizes the quartets are drawn from.

For more information about likelihood-mapping refer to
 - Schmidt and von Haeseler (2009) The Phylogenetic Handbook, 2nd Ed.
   (by Lemey et al., Eds.), 181-209, Cambridge Univ. Press, UK.
   http://www.thephylogenetichandbook.org
